WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.968
In the city of Jinling, thirty-year-old Li Yu ascended the throne; he loved writing poetry, but he did not like managing the affairs of state.

00:00:08.318 --> 00:00:14.702
The Song dynasty in the north grew stronger and stronger, and its great army pressed toward Southern Tang step by step.

00:00:15.052 --> 00:00:21.652
In the year 975, Song troops surrounded Jinling, and the people in the city were filled with fear.

00:00:22.002 --> 00:00:28.266
The common people hid in their homes, praying the war would end soon.

00:00:28.616 --> 00:00:33.656
Li Yu had no strength to resist and could only surrender; Southern Tang thus perished.

00:00:34.006 --> 00:00:39.574
The gates of Jinling slowly opened, and a dynasty came to its end.

00:00:39.924 --> 00:00:45.756
He was taken to the capital in the north, changed from a king into a prisoner.

00:00:46.106 --> 00:00:52.322
Though he failed in politics, his poetry has been handed down through the ages, and people remember him forever.

00:00:52.672 --> 00:00:57.616
His story reminds later generations that governing a country cannot rely on talent alone.

